# TypeScript/JavaScript Patterns

> This file extends [common/patterns.mdc](../common/patterns.mdc) with TypeScript/JavaScript specific content.

## API Response Format

```typescript
type ApiResponse<T> =
  | { ok: true; data: T }
  | { ok: false; error: { code: string; message: string } }
```

## Custom Hooks Pattern

```typescript
export function useDebounce<T>(value: T, delay: number): T {
  const [debouncedValue, setDebouncedValue] = useState<T>(value)

  useEffect(() => {
    const handler = setTimeout(() => setDebouncedValue(value), delay)
    return () => clearTimeout(handler)
  }, [value, delay])

  return debouncedValue
}
```

## Versioned Boundary Contracts

```typescript
type QueryWorkerMessage =
  | { version: 1; requestId: string; type: 'query'; query: FindingQuery }
  | { version: 1; requestId: string; type: 'export'; query: FindingQuery }

function parseQueryWorkerMessage(value: unknown): QueryWorkerMessage {
  return queryWorkerMessageSchema.parse(value)
}
```

Keep stream, API, URL, preference, and worker-message contracts explicit,
versioned, and validated. Use discriminated unions for protocols and exhaust
all variants. Do not model immutable dataset versions or Finding Blocks as a
mutable CRUD repository.
